# dns-monitor

A console application for the monitoring of DNS communication on a network interface or from a `.pcap` file.

## Description

The main aim of this application is to monitor DNS communication on a given interface or to parse a `.pcap` file and print the communication to the console. The application also provides the option to write all the domain names and or the domain name to IP translations to a file output.

### Attention

Records that are not of type `A`, `AAAA`, `NS`, `MX`, `SOA`, `CNAME`, or `SRV` are ignored in the resource records sections of verbose output.


## Usage

```
./dns-monitor (-i <interface> | -p <pcapfile>) [-v] [-d <domainsfile>] [-t <translationsfile>]
```

Arguments:
- `-i <interface>` - the name of the interface to listen on, or
- `-p <pcapfile>` - the name of the `.pcap` file to parse;
- `-v` - "verbose" mode: complete information output of the DNS messages;
- `-d <domainsfile>` - the name of the domain names file;
- `-t <translationsfile>` - the name of the domain name to IP address translations file.

### Examples

```
./dns-monitor -i eth0
2024-09-17 14:42:10 192.168.1.5 -> 8.8.8.8 (Q 1/0/0/0)
2024-09-17 14:42:11 8.8.8.8 -> 192.168.1.5 (R 1/1/2/2)
```

```
./dns-monitor -i eth0 -v
Timestamp: 2024-09-17 14:42:10
SrcIP: 192.168.1.5
DstIP: 8.8.8.8
SrcPort: UDP/54321
DstPort: UDP/53
Identifier: 0xA1B2
Flags: QR=0, OPCODE=0, AA=0, TC=0, RD=1, RA=0, AD=0, CD=0, RCODE=0

[Question Section]
google.com. IN A.
====================

Timestamp: 2024-09-17 14:42:11
SrcIP: 8.8.8.8
DstIP: 192.168.1.5
SrcPort: UDP/53
DstPort: UDP/54321
Identifier: 0xA1B2
Flags: QR=1, OPCODE=0, AA=1, TC=0, RD=1, RA=1, AD=0, CD=0, RCODE=0

[Question Section]
google.com. IN A

[Answer Section]
google.com. 300 IN A 142.250.183.142

[Authority Section]
google.com. 86400 IN NS ns1.google.com.
google.com. 86400 IN NS ns2.google.com.

[Additional Section]
ns1.google.com. 86400 IN A 216.239.32.10
ns2.google.com. 86400 IN A 216.239.34.10
```


